    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0132" n="64" xml:id="pg64"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1933.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date ana="#date_apparent-typo-based-on-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1867-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 15,
                        1857</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 25th of January, No. 1307, which relates to Mr. Dudley as the
                    person named to succeed Mr. Morse in the charge of any unfinished business
                    pertaining to the Treasury Department, and to inform you that proper
                    instructions have been addressed to Mr. Dudley on the subject by this
                    department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
